
===== STAGE 1 · COLLECT  (🤖 read-only — a script may do this unattended) =====
  captured diagnostics from the host, read-only, in: <repo>/lab/agent/docs05-rowsT.1-T.2/fixture
    catalog-curl.txt
    console-record.txt
    fdesetup.txt
    keychain-identity.txt
    profiles-list.txt
    profiles-status.txt
  bundle assembled (35 lines). NOT sent anywhere — that is a person's act.

===== STAGE 2 · CLASSIFY  (🤖 a model names the probable cause with its evidence line) =====
  The USB-restriction setting is not in effect because its configuration profile (com.lab.restrictions.usb), which the management server records as deployed, is absent from the device's installed-profile list, as shown by console-record.txt (server lists four scoped profiles incl. com.lab.restrictions.usb) and profiles-list.txt (only three local profiles; com.lab.restrictions.usb not among them).

===== STAGE 3 · PROPOSE  (🤖 name the remediation from docs/05 — 🔴 mark what a person must gate) =====
  symptom class: docs/05 · B — a profile applied in the console but not in effect
    🤖 automatable: re-push the profile (reversible — the payload replaces itself)
    🤖 automatable: re-check the device with 'profiles list' afterwards (read-only)
    🔴 GATE (a person): if it is a non-removable profile, do NOT unset it — that is a future wipe
    🔴 GATE (a person): if the host has not checked in, decide re-enrolment — which on a supervised Mac is a wipe

===== STAGE 4 · THE GATE  (🔴 nothing above changed the host; a person decides from here) =====
  Proposed, not run. A person confirms the 🔴 items and runs them.
  Severity and the trigger to remediate stay with a person by design (ledger T.3, ⛔).
  Rule: the line is the cost of being wrong on THIS machine, not the difficulty of the command.
